# netsurf: drop shadows and transformed boxes are no longer clipped to their own box
# Generated 2026-09-22
#
# The core clipped a box's background paint to the box, so the drop-shadow
# rect (patch 26) and the transformed quad (patch 27) that the plotters draw
# outside the border box were cut off (PM-shadow showed 1px of an 8px shadow;
# MacSurf's own renderer honours the same clip). Two parts, both needed:
# - html/box_ink.h (new, header-only): the ink outset of a box's background
#   paint -- shadow offset clamped +/-16 like the plotters; the transformed
#   quad's bounds (exact for a static angle, circumscribed circle for an
#   animated one).
# - layout.c layout_get_box_bbox: include the box's own ink, so every
#   ancestor's redraw clip (a descendant bbox) contains it.
# - redraw.c html_redraw_box: widen the clip around the background paint to
#   border box + ink, bounded by the parent's clip, so the box's own
#   overflow:hidden does not cut its own shadow; a CSS clip: rect still does.
# Only CLIP lines change in the plot stream; L1 canary SAME.
# See docs/phase-0/09-vita-frontend.md §10.

